  "mechanism": {
    "example": "Earn 20,000 piastres as current-period DailyWage; standalone handler pays that amount and records Settlement debit. Payroll creation includes period ledger rows but PayrollRules ignores Settlement, so the frozen line remains 20,000. Paying the run posts another 20,000 treasury outflow and PayrollSettlement; projected ledger balance becomes -20,000.",
    "static_arithmetic_only": true
  },
  "counterevidence_and_limits": [
    "Ledger types intentionally remain distinct and each path has separate permissions; business intent may define mutually exclusive modes, but inspected routes/handlers do not enforce exclusivity.",
    "Payroll snapshots freeze at create time; standalone payment after creation leaves the frozen line unchanged.",
    "No database-backed scenario or owner policy confirmation was performed.",
    "Inspected tests cover each payment path separately, not the combined sequence."
  ],
